{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not be</b> — this is the advice." "<b>Like a horse, like a mule</b> — a way of elegance, without vav: כרע כאח לי, and sometimes the kaf is omitted. Rabbi Moses said: Do not be like the likeness of a horse, which needs a bit and bridle, and he said עדיו is like לחיו (his jaws), and similar to it המשביע בטוב עדייך." "<b>To restrain</b> — a word known in the language of the Sages." "And the meaning of לבל קרוב אליך — to harm you." "And some say: כי בל קרוב אליך — far be it from you to be like a horse, in the manner of: ועצת רשעם רחקה מני (Job 10:3)." "And some say: that the word אותו is missing, as if it were written: במתג ורסן תפארתו, לבלום אותו." "And further: עדיו — in the manner of: למצוא עונו לשנוא (Lamentations 2:14)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {6 "The phrase למצוא עונו לשנוא is cited from Lamentations 2:14; Ibn Ezra draws the analogy based on the root עדה/עון."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:18.419958096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}